Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/decomposition/_dict_learning.py:dict_learning_online`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 738 | def dict_learning_online(\n 739 |     X,\n 740 |     n_components=2,\n 741 |     *,\n 742 |     alpha=1,\n 743 |     n_iter=\"deprecated\",\n 744 |     max_iter=None,\n 745 |     return_code=True,\n 746 |     dict_init=None,\n 747 |     callback=None,\n 748 |     batch_size=\"warn\",\n 749 |     verbose=False,\n 750 |     shuffle=True,\n 751 |     n_jobs=None,\n 752 |     method=\"lars\",\n 753 |     iter_offset=\"deprecated\",\n 754 |     random_state=None,\n 755 |     return_inner_stats=\"deprecated\",\n 756 |     inner_stats=\"deprecated\",\n 757 |     return_n_iter=\"deprecated\",\n 758 |     positive_dict=False,\n 759 |     positive_code=False,\n 760 |     method_max_iter=1000,\n 761 |     tol=1e-3,\n 762 |     max_no_improvement=10,\n 763 | ):\n 764 |     \"\"\"Solves a dictionary learning matrix factorization problem online.\n 765 | \n 766 |     Finds the best dictionary and the corresponding sparse code for\n 767 |     approximating the data matrix X by solving::\n 768 | \n 769 |         (U^*, V^*) = argmin 0.5 || X - U V ||_Fro^2 + alpha * || U ||_1,1\n 770 |                      (U,V)\n 771 |                      with || V_k ||_2 = 1 for all  0 <= k < n_components\n 772 | \n 773 |     where V is the dictionary and U is the sparse code. ||.||_Fro stands for\n 774 |     the Frobenius norm and ||.||_1,1 stands for the entry-wise matrix norm\n 775 |     which is the sum of the absolute values of all the entries in the matrix.\n 776 |     This is accomplished by repeatedly iterating over mini-batches by slicing\n 777 |     the input data.\n 778 | \n 779 |     Read more in the :ref:`User Guide <DictionaryLearning>`.\n 780 | \n 781 |     Parameters\n 782 |     ----------\n 783 |     X : ndarray of shape (n_samples, n_features)\n 784 |         Data matrix.\n 785 | \n 786 |     n_components : int or None,