ad(AB):\n501 |         # gradient of the objective function\n502 |         P = expit(-(AB[0] * F + AB[1]))\n503 |         TEP_minus_T1P = T - P\n504 |         if sample_weight is not None:\n505 |             TEP_minus_T1P *= sample_weight\n506 |         dA = np.dot(TEP_minus_T1P, F)\n507 |         dB = np.sum(TEP_minus_T1P)\n508 |         return np.array([dA, dB])\n509 | \n510 |     AB0 = np.array([0., log((prior0 + 1.) / (prior1 + 1.))])\n511 |     AB_ = fmin_bfgs(objective, AB0, fprime=grad, disp=False)\n512 |     return AB_[0], AB_[1]\n```\n\nFound file `sklearn/linear_model/_base.py`.\nFound file `sklearn/linear_model/_bayes.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Use more detailed query to get the full content of some if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"hashlib.md5\", \"validate_checksum hashlib.md5\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `sklearn/datasets/_base.py:_pkl_filepath`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1127 | def _pkl_filepath(*args, **kwargs):\n1128 |     \"\"\"Return filename for Python 3 pickles\n1129 | \n1130 |     args[-1] is expected to be the \".pkl\" filename. For compatibility with\n1131 |     older scikit-learn versions, a suffix is inserted before the extension.\n1132 | \n1133 |     _pkl_filepath('/path/to/folder', 'filename.pkl') returns\n1134 |     '/path/to/folder/filename_py3.pkl'\n1135 | \n1136 |     \"\"\"\n1137 |     py3_suffix = kwargs.get(\"py3_suffix\", \"_py3\")\n1138 |     basename, ext = splitext(args[-1])\n1139 |     basename += py3_suffix\n1140 |     new_args = args[:-1] + (basename + ext,)\n1141 |     return join(*new_args)\n```\n\nFound function `sklearn/datasets/_base.py:_sha256`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1144 | def _sha256(path):\n1145 |     \"\"\"Calculate the sha256 hash of the file at path.\"\"\"\n1146 |     sha256hash = hashlib.sha256()\n1147 |     chunk_size = 8192\n1148 |     with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n1