 |         if hasattr(cls, name):\n286 |             warnings.warn(\n287 |                 f\"registration of accessor {accessor!r} under name \"\n288 |                 f\"{name!r} for type {cls!r} is overriding a preexisting \"\n289 |                 f\"attribute with the same name.\",\n290 |                 UserWarning,\n291 |                 stacklevel=find_stack_level(),\n292 |             )\n293 |         setattr(cls, name, Accessor(name, accessor))\n294 |         cls._accessors.add(name)\n295 |         return accessor\n296 | \n297 |     return decorator\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/core/accessor.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/core/accessor.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"Can only use .str accessor with string values! str accessor\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/core/strings/accessor.py:_get_group_names`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n3824 | def _get_group_names(regex: re.Pattern) -> list[Hashable] | range:\n3825 |     \"\"\"\n3826 |     Get named groups from compiled regex.\n3827 | \n3828 |     Unnamed groups are numbered.\n3829 | \n3830 |     Parameters\n3831 |     ----------\n3832 |     regex : compiled regex\n3833 | \n3834 |     Returns\n3835 |     -------\n3836 |     list of column labels\n3837 |     \"\"\"\n3838 |     rng = range(regex.groups)\n3839 |     names = {v: k for k, v in regex.groupindex.items()}\n3840 |     if not names:\n3841 |         return rng\n3842 |     result: list[Hashable] = [names.get(1 + i, i) for i in rng]\n3843 |     arr = np.array(result)\n3844 |     if arr.dtype.kind == \"i\" and lib.is_range_indexer(arr, len(arr)):\n3845 |         return rng\n3846 |     return result\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/core/arrays/categorical.py:CategoricalAccessor._validate`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2924 | def _validate(data) -> None:\n2925 |         if not isinstance(data.dtype