or Series (if level specified)\n6992 |             Median of the values for the requested axis.\n6993 | \n6994 |         See Also\n6995 |         --------\n6996 |         numpy.median : Equivalent numpy function for computing median.\n6997 |         Series.sum : Sum of the values.\n6998 |         Series.median : Median of the values.\n6999 |         Series.std : Standard deviation of the values.\n7000 |         Series.var : Variance of the values.\n7001 |         Series.min : Minimum value.\n7002 |         Series.max : Maximum value.\n7003 | \n7004 |         Examples\n7005 |         --------\n7006 |         >>> s = pd.Series([1, 2, 3])\n7007 |         >>> s.median()\n7008 |         2.0\n7009 | \n7010 |         With a DataFrame\n7011 | \n7012 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1, 2], \"b\": [2, 3]}, index=[\"tiger\", \"zebra\"])\n7013 |         >>> df\n7014 |                a   b\n7015 |         tiger  1   2\n7016 |         zebra  2   3\n7017 |         >>> df.median()\n7018 |         a   1.5\n7019 |         b   2.5\n7020 |         dtype: float64\n7021 | \n7022 |         Using axis=1\n7023 | \n7024 |         >>> df.median(axis=1)\n7025 |         tiger   1.5\n7026 |         zebra   2.5\n7027 |         dtype: float64\n7028 | \n7029 |         In this case, `numeric_only` should be set to `True`\n7030 |         to avoid getting an error.\n7031 | \n7032 |         >>> df = pd.DataFrame({\"a\": [1, 2], \"b\": [\"T\", \"Z\"]}, index=[\"tiger\", \"zebra\"])\n7033 |         >>> df.median(numeric_only=True)\n7034 |         a   1.5\n7035 |         dtype: float64\n7036 |         \"\"\"\n7037 |         return NDFrame.median(\n7038 |             self, axis=axis, skipna=skipna, numeric_only=numeric_only, **kwargs\n7039 |         )\n7040 | \n7041 |     @deprecate_nonkeyword_arguments(version=\"4.0\", allowed_args=[\"self\"], name=\"sem\")\n7042 |     @doc(make_doc(\"sem\", ndim=1))\n7043 |     def sem(\n7044 |         self,\n7045 |         axis: Axis | None = None,\n7046 |      