code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1571 | def walk(self, where: str = \"/\") -> Iterator[tuple[str, list[str], list[str]]]:\n1572 |         \"\"\"\n1573 |         Walk the pytables group hierarchy for pandas objects.\n1574 | \n1575 |         This generator will yield the group path, subgroups and pandas object\n1576 |         names for each group.\n1577 | \n1578 |         Any non-pandas PyTables objects that are not a group will be ignored.\n1579 | \n1580 |         The `where` group itself is listed first (preorder), then each of its\n1581 |         child groups (following an alphanumerical order) is also traversed,\n1582 |         following the same procedure.\n1583 | \n1584 |         Parameters\n1585 |         ----------\n1586 |         where : str, default \"/\"\n1587 |             Group where to start walking.\n1588 | \n1589 |         Yields\n1590 |         ------\n1591 |         path : str\n1592 |             Full path to a group (without trailing '/').\n1593 |         groups : list\n1594 |             Names (strings) of the groups contained in `path`.\n1595 |         leaves : list\n1596 |             Names (strings) of the pandas objects contained in `path`.\n1597 | \n1598 |         See Also\n1599 |         --------\n1600 |         HDFStore.info : Prints detailed information on the store.\n1601 | \n1602 |         Examples\n1603 |         --------\n1604 |         >>> df1 = pd.DataFrame([[1, 2], [3, 4]], columns=[\"A\", \"B\"])\n1605 |         >>> store = pd.HDFStore(\"store.h5\", \"w\")  # doctest: +SKIP\n1606 |         >>> store.put(\"data\", df1, format=\"table\")  # doctest: +SKIP\n1607 |         >>> df2 = pd.DataFrame([[5, 6], [7, 8]], columns=[\"A\", \"B\"])\n1608 |         >>> store.append(\"data\", df2)  # doctest: +SKIP\n1609 |         >>> store.close()  # doctest: +SKIP\n1610 |         >>> for group in store.walk():  # doctest: +SKIP\n1611 |         ...     print(group)  # doctest: +SKIP\n1612 |         >>> store.close()  # doctest: +SKIP\n1613 |         \"\"\"\n1614 |         _tables()\n1615 |         self._check_if_open()\n1616 |         assert self._handle is not None  # for mypy\n1617 |         assert _table_mod is not None  # for mypy\n1618 | \n1619 |         for g in self._handle.walk_groups(where):\n1620 |             if getattr(g._v_attrs, \"pandas_type\", None) is not None:\n1621 |                 continue\n1622 | \n1623 |             groups = []\n1624 |             leaves = []\n1625 |             for child in g._v_children.values():\n1626 |                 pandas_type = getattr(child._v_attrs, \"pandas_type\", None)\n1627 |                 if pandas_type is None:\n1628 |                     if isinstance(child, _table_mod.group.Group):\n1629 |                         groups.append(child._v_name)\n1630 |                 else:\n1631 |                     leaves.append(child._v_name)\n1632 | \n1633 |             yield (g._v_pathname.rstrip(\"/\"), groups, leaves)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/io/pytables.py:Fixed.pandas_type`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2802 | def pandas_type(self):\n2803 |         return getattr(self.group._v_attrs, \"pandas_type\", None)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/io/pytables.py:Fixed.set_object_info`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2816 | def set_object_info(self) -> None:\n2817 |         \"\"\"set my pandas type & version\"\"\"\n2818 |         self.attrs.pandas_type = str(self.pandas_kind)\n2819 |         self.attrs.pandas_version = str(_version)\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/io/pytables.py:Fixed._handle`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2834 | def _handle(self):\n2835 |         return self.parent._handle\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/io/pytables.py:Fixed.set_attrs`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n2853 | def set_attrs(self) -> None:\n2854 |         \"\"\"set our object attributes\"\"\"\n```\n\nFound function `pandas/io/pytables